 ## Desktop agent
+
+### Professional connectivity and content-management options
+
+The Engine exposes the service-level equivalents of the Kosmos-Oden settings
+panels. Host applications may present different controls, but they must retain
+the same security boundaries and report unavailable capabilities truthfully.
+
+| Option family | Engine capability | Current status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Agent API (HTTP + MCP) | Authenticated, sensitivity-filtered local graph, notes, Graphiti, health, capability, event, and MCP surfaces | Implemented incrementally; the released desktop-agent endpoints listed below remain the conservative public baseline |
+| Quick Connect MCP | Stable endpoint and credential contract suitable for vendor-neutral Streamable HTTP and first-party stdio adapters | Protocol foundation implemented; polished Anthropic, OpenAI, and universal configuration generators are a host/product responsibility until separately shipped and tested |
+| GKOS note formatting | GKX 2.2/2.3 parsing, validation, safe migration plans, timestamp validation, exclusions, hash-bound preview, backup/apply boundaries, and proposal-only enrichment | Implemented library and CLI primitives; automatic host-file stamping requires an authorized host adapter |
+| Vault synchronization | Provider-neutral synchronization must preserve source bytes, serialize runs, use per-replica checkpoints, detect conflicts, and make deletion propagation explicit | Nextcloud/WebDAV transport, startup scheduling, multi-provider fan-out, and production conflict recovery are not Engine capabilities today |
+
+A professional host must additionally provide secret-store integration,
+loopback-by-default binding, explicit LAN disclosure, credential rotation,
+connection testing, health reporting, bounded retries, redacted diagnostics,
+and truthful capability discovery. A bearer token proves possession only; it
+does not establish agent identity, user identity, approval, or write authority.
+
+The Engine will not silently emulate synchronization by copying directories.
+Any future sync provider must define replica identity, conflict and deletion
+semantics, crash recovery, credential handling, checkpoints, and auditable
+receipts before it is advertised as available.
 
